    {
      "id": "claim_ba94cfe097d6421f93ccfcfa447590eb",
      "statement": "brijio install [--ws-port N] [--mcp-port N] creates ~/.brijio/ with a mode-0600 .env (tokens generated on first install and preserved on reinstall, ports optionally overridden), a bin/brijio shell wrapper exec'ing the resolved binary, and a platform service definition symlinked into the OS location: a macOS LaunchAgent plist (com.redvex.brijio, RunAtLoad/KeepAlive true, WorkingDirectory ~/.brijio) loaded via launchctl, or a Linux systemd user unit (Restart=on-failure, EnvironmentFile=%h/.brijio/.env, WantedBy=default.target) enabled via systemctl --user. Daemon support is darwin/linux only.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/architecture/decisions/0037-daemon-install-via-npx.md",
