    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dece0abb3a71416b83824fdcb0471595",
      "statement": "The release workflow attaches extension assets to the vX.Y.Z release: Chrome (ubuntu) builds @brijio/chrome-extension, validates dist/manifest.json version equals the release version, and uploads brijio-chrome-extension-<version>.zip. Safari (macos-latest) builds @brijio/safari-extension, validates iOS/macOS manifest versions, uploads web-extension ZIPs, and runs xcrun safari-web-extension-converter (continue-on-error) to produce Xcode project ZIPs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/tag-and-release.yml#L120-L250",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8adfbc733331ca690ab3e8fdf23c2baf8290dc69eaee6d2261abfe045027b2ca:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/tag-and-release.yml#L250-L330",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:63803f1e48e12980b94bafb86a498b97d200b15f9228bfb0dd4553253caebed7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5974112bd82c4663b95d760836a2dd50",
      "statement": "When Apple Developer ID secrets are configured, the Safari release job builds a signed, notarized, stapled Brijio.app: imports a .p12 into a temporary keychain, xcodebuilds with manual code signing and a secure timestamp, submits via xcrun notarytool submit --wait verifying status is Accepted, staples the ticket (retried up to 5 times for CloudKit propagation), and uploads brijio-safari-macos-<version>.zip. Without signing secrets only the unsigned Xcode project ZIPs are uploaded.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/tag-and-release.yml#L330-L475",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8b9a8e45e1482fbcbebf24f9ef532111d5ddf71966d53e3d9c0d0cd8e193f059:"
        },
        {
